Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
TwistedBS: Original Mathematica Calculations for E2, E3, and S9-S13\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"75bcd35f-a8b3-9b4a-8f84-356ae2fa454c"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook assembles selected Input cells from the original notebooks, \
retaining the original variable names, models, Fourier fits, matrix \
construction, eigensystem calculations, unfolded spectra, and Wilson-loop \
algorithms. It does not call TwistedBS_figures.wl.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6072ba12-8402-404d-a6ce-dc33aaef126f"],

Cell["\<\
The 3+1 calculation uses a single twist angle, with theta31=1 degree by \
default. E2, S10, and S11 share these cells; change the angle and rerun the \
section to select another case. E3 and S13 each use a fixed angle of 1 \
degree. S12 reads existing per-angle CSV files without calculating additional \
angles.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31dc8074-5ef8-1e4a-96e5-a99b331c762e"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate the sections in order. S12 requires peakfit - Sheet1.csv and the \
spectrum different angle folder in the same directory as this notebook. All \
model definitions and unfolding functions are embedded.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f475f022-8975-a048-995d-83a0423eed88"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["0. Parameters and Original Model Definitions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3aa3ea1a-492c-c945-a279-e10458f587e6"],

Cell["\<\
theta31 is the single 3+1 twist angle in degrees. moireShell retains the \
original value of 5. Evaluate in a fresh kernel.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3628b71b-9a68-134d-9939-3a3142c37b59"],

